## Why This Is Asked

Tests a beginner's ability to design a practical, auditable maintenance workflow using familiar AWS services with least-privilege access.

## Key Concepts

- AWS Systems Manager Run Command
- IAM roles with trust relationships and least privilege
- CloudWatch Logs and CloudTrail for audit trails
- AWS SSO integration for role assumption
- Minimal IaC (Terraform) to create roles and SSM associations

## Code Example

```terraform
# Terraform snippet creating cross-account SAPOperator role and IAM policy
provider "aws" { region = "us-east-1" }

# Role
resource "aws_iam_role" "sap_operator" {
  name = "SAPOperator"
  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17",
    Statement = [{
      Effect = "Allow",
      Principal = { AWS = "arn:aws:iam::ACCOUNT_ID:saml-provider/AWS_SSO" },
      Action = "sts:AssumeRole"
    }]
  })
}

# Policy
resource "aws_iam_policy" "sap_operator_policy" {
  name = "SAPOperatorPolicy"
  policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17",
    Statement = [
      { Effect = "Allow", Action = ["ssm:SendCommand","ssm:ListCommands","ssm:DescribeInstanceInformation"], Resource = "*" },
      { Effect = "Allow", Action = ["logs:CreateLogGroup","logs:CreateLogStream","logs:PutLogEvents"], Resource = "*" }
    ]
  })
}

resource "aws_iam_role_policy_attachment" "attach" {
  role       = aws_iam_role.sap_operator.name
  policy_arn = aws_iam_policy.sap_operator_policy.arn
}
```

```terraform
# SSM association to run healthcheck on SAP EC2
data "aws_ssm_document" "run_shell" { name = "AWS-RunShellScript" }

resource "aws_ssm_association" "healthcheck" {
  name            = data.aws_ssm_document.run_shell.name
  instance_id     = "<SAP_EC2_INSTANCE_ID>"
  parameters = {
    commands = ["bash /usr/local/bin/healthcheck.sh"]
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
This tests cross-account policy design for SAP-to-SageMaker integration with JIT, MFA, and auditability.

## Key Concepts
- Tag-based principal mapping
- Least privilege IAM policies for SageMaker
- STS with MFA for ephemeral creds
- CloudTrail audit and GitOps IaC

## Code Example
```yaml
# Terraform-like snippet illustrating the cross-account role and trust
provider "aws" { region = "us-east-1" }
resource "aws_iam_role" "sap_bridge" {
  name = "sap-sagemaker-bridge"
  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    "Version": "2012-10-17",
    "Statement": [{
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Principal": {"Federated": "arn:aws:iam::123456789012:saml-provider/sap"},
      "Action": "sts:AssumeRole"
    }]
  })
}
resource "aws_iam_role_policy" "sap_bridge_policy" {
  role   = aws_iam_role.sap_bridge.id
  policy = jsonencode({
    "Version": "2012-10-17",
    "Statement": [{
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": ["sagemaker:InvokeEndpoint"],
      "Resource": "arn:aws:sagemaker:us-east-1:111122223333:endpoint/my-endpoint"
    }]
  })
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you enforce per-SAP-object granularity if multiple SAP subsystems share a SageMaker endpoint?
- How would you test for drift and unauthorized access attempts?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests cross‑account trust, JIT elevation, SAP/IAM mapping, and auditable credential management with Secrets Manager and cross‑region replication.

## Key Concepts
- Cross‑account IAM roles and STS
- Service Control Policies
- Secrets Manager rotation and replication
- Just‑In‑Time elevation
- Auditing with CloudTrail/CloudWatch
- AWS SSO MFA gating

## Code Example
```javascript
// CloudFormation-like snippet (translatable to YAML)
{
  "AWSTemplateFormatVersion": "2010-09-09",
  "Resources": {
    "SAPCrossAccountRole": {
      "Type": "AWS::IAM::Role",
      "Properties": {
        "RoleName": "SAPCrossAccountRole",
        "AssumeRolePolicyDocument": {
          "Version": "2012-10-17",
          "Statement": [
            {
              "Effect": "Allow",
              "Principal": {"AWS": "arn:aws:iam::<SHARED_ACCOUNT_ID>:root"},
              "Action": "sts:AssumeRole"
            }
          ]
        },
        "Policies": [
          {
            "PolicyName": "SAPAccess",
            "PolicyDocument": {
              "Version": "2012-10-17",
              "Statement": [
                {"Effect": "Allow", "Action": ["ec2:Describe*","s3:GetObject","logs:CreateLogStream"], "Resource": "*"}
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  }
}
```

